  "name": "Padel Park - WhatsApp & Instagram AI Agent template",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5a74e441-c440-4e7b-85cf-dcc654f5dc3f",
      "name": "Workflow Overview & Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1040,
        1216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#B6AF95",
        "width": 950,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "# WhatsApp + Instagram AI Customer Assistant\n\n**Purpose**\nReceives incoming WhatsApp and Instagram messages, identifies the sender, checks whether staff have taken over, asks OpenAI to classify the request, then sends a reply and logs the conversation. Corporate/group enquiries are saved as leads and emailed to staff. Requests needing a person trigger a staff alert and a temporary quiet period.\n\n**Before you activate**\n1. **OpenAI:** connect your API credential in `Generate AI Intent & Reply` and replace every `[PLACEHOLDER]` in its system prompt with your own business details.\n2. **WhatsApp:** connect WhatsApp Business Cloud API in `Send WhatsApp Reply` and replace `YOUR_WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`.\n3. **Instagram:** set your business account ID in `Normalize Message`; add your access token and account ID in `Send Instagram Reply`.\n4. **Google Sheets:** connect your account and select your spreadsheet in every Sheets node. Create the `Contacts`, `Leads`, and `Conversations` tabs with the column headers described in the setup note.\n5. **Email:** connect SMTP and replace the sender/staff email placeholders in both staff email nodes.\n6. **Meta webhooks:** configure both POST message endpoints and both GET verification endpoints using the webhook URLs from your active n8n instance.\n\n**Important**\nThis workflow sends real replies and staff emails, and writes to your spreadsheet. Test with your own accounts before production. The assistant only knows the business information you provide in its system prompt."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "71a830ab-4629-4421-9fa8-780a9f4362a6",
      "name": "1. Receive & Normalize Messages",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        48,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 110,
        "content": "**1 \u00b7 Receive & normalize**\nTwo POST webhooks receive WhatsApp and Instagram events. `Normalize Message` extracts the platform, sender ID, message text/type, and media reference; non-message Instagram events and echoes are ignored."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "502f0cf2-2f5d-485e-8628-bfd231b1dfa7",
      "name": "2. Contact Lookup & Welcome",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        784,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 110,
        "content": "**2 \u00b7 Identify the contact**\n`Lookup Contact` searches the Contacts sheet by `sender_id`. New contacts receive a welcome reply and are added to the sheet; existing contacts continue through the handoff-status check."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "47ff06ec-9597-440c-8668-1cef795e4ea6",
      "name": "3. Human Handoff Guard",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1488,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 600,
        "height": 110,
        "content": "**3 \u00b7 Respect staff handoff**\nThe workflow checks `status` and `handoff_time`. If a contact is marked `handed_off` within the configured 4-hour window, the workflow stops without an AI reply. Staff can restore `status` to `active` to resume replies."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1d8d7777-fc7e-4dab-ac4e-a43dbc7bba9b",
      "name": "4. AI Intent & Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2240,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 110,
        "content": "**4 \u00b7 Classify and route the request**\nOpenAI returns JSON with an intent and reply. `Parse AI Response` parses it, then `Route by Intent` sends corporate/group enquiries to lead capture, human requests to staff handoff, and other requests to the normal reply path. Keep the prompt\u2019s intent names aligned with the Switch rules."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2191bb30-9e0a-412d-ba0b-26bbf9b034e7",
      "name": "5. Lead Capture & Staff Alerts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2944,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 610,
        "height": 110,
        "content": "**5 \u00b7 Capture leads and alert staff**\nCorporate/group/event enquiries are checked for name and contact details. Complete leads are appended to `Leads` and emailed to staff. Human handoff updates the contact status/time and sends a staff email. Review both email nodes before testing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "92cc9d50-45bc-4d2f-ae49-5a37d9570823",
      "name": "6. Send Replies & Log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3664,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 610,
        "height": 110,
        "content": "**6 \u00b7 Send the response and log it**\n`Which Platform?` routes the reply to WhatsApp or Instagram. Both send paths feed `Log Conversation`, which records timestamp, platform, sender, message, intent, and reply in `Conversations`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "abf97005-3681-4ee0-a9a4-b957bb573970",
      "name": "Webhook Verification Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1920,
        1888
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#E4D0B8",
        "width": 800,
        "height": 500,
        "content": "## Meta webhook verification\n\nThe GET webhook nodes are separate from the POST message receivers:\n- `WhatsApp Webhook (GET - Verify)` \u2192 `Respond to Meta Verify`\n- `Instagram Webhook (GET - Verify)` \u2192 `Respond to Meta Verify`\n\nIn Meta, use the corresponding n8n webhook URL and the same verification token you configure in Meta. The response node returns `hub.challenge` when supplied; verify each app subscription independently. Use the production webhook URL and activate the workflow before relying on live events."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "854b8f89-d112-45bf-bfff-97ea9c5df31b",
      "name": "Spreadsheet Structure & Testing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        736,
        1856
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#B6AF95",
        "width": 1050,
        "height": 550,
        "content": "## Google Sheets structure & test checklist\n\n**Contacts** \u2014 `sender_id`, `platform`, `first_seen`, `status`, `handoff_time`.\n\n**Leads** \u2014 `timestamp`, `platform`, `sender_id`, `name`, `contact`, `group_size`, `date`, `purpose`, `status`.\n\n**Conversations** \u2014 `timestamp`, `platform`, `sender_id`, `message`, `reply`, `intent`.\n\n**Test before publishing**\n1. Send a first-time message on each platform and check the welcome path.\n2. Send a returning-contact message and confirm AI routing works.\n3. Test a corporate/group enquiry with complete and incomplete details.\n4. Test a human handoff; confirm the contact is marked `handed_off` and replies are suppressed during the 4-hour window.\n5. Confirm each reply and intent is logged to the correct spreadsheet tab.\n\nUse the exact column names above. Re-select the correct spreadsheet and worksheet in each Google Sheets node after importing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a6051225-ccce-4613-8014-060f2b972587",
      "name": "Demo Video & Walkthrough",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3632,
        1824
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#E4D0B8",
        "width": 420,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "## Workflow demo\n[Watch the demo video](https://youtu.be/QEovtlc_9-A)\n\nThe video demonstrates the workflow behaviour. Set up your own Meta, OpenAI, Google Sheets, and SMTP credentials before testing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b7166b7a-911b-4163-a408-7e9e6507c157",
      "name": "Respond to Meta Verify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "position": [
        368,
        2016
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "respondWith": "text",
        "responseBody": "={{ $json.query && $json.query['hub.challenge'] ? $json.query['hub.challenge'] : 'ok' }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "23813a84-4852-451a-8d64-febaaafbb99a",
      "name": "Normalize Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        368,
        1312
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const OUR_INSTAGRAM_ID = 'YOUR_INSTAGRAM_BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ID';\n\nconst body = $json.body || $json;\nlet platform = null, senderId = null, messageType = null, messageText = '', mediaId = '';\n\ntry {\n  if (body.entry && body.entry[0].changes) {\n    const value = body.entry[0].changes[0].value;\n    const msg = value.messages ? value.messages[0] : null;\n    if (!msg) { return []; }\n    platform = 'whatsapp';\n    senderId = msg.from;\n    messageType = msg.type;\n    if (messageType === 'text') {\n      messageText = msg.text.body;\n    } else if (messageType === 'audio') {\n      mediaId = msg.audio.id;\n    }\n  } else if (body.entry && body.entry[0].messaging) {\n    const messaging = body.entry[0].messaging[0];\n\n    // Only process genuine incoming messages. Skip everything else:\n    // read receipts, delivery receipts, reactions, echoes (no \"message\" field, or is_echo true).\n    if (!messaging.message || messaging.message.is_echo) {\n      return [];\n    }\n\n    platform = 'instagram';\n    senderId = messaging.sender.id;\n    if (messaging.message.text) {\n      messageType = 'text';\n      messageText = messaging.message.text;\n    } else if (messaging.message.attachments && messaging.message.attachments[0]) {\n      const att = messaging.message.attachments[0];\n      messageType = att.type;\n      mediaId = att.payload ? att.payload.url : '';\n    }\n  } else {\n    return [];\n  }\n} catch (e) {\n  return [];\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: { platform, senderId, messageType, messageText, mediaId } }];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
